WEBVTT

00:01:29.454 --> 00:01:31.621
It actually takes a lot
of computational power

00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:33.746
to make neural networks
able to really sing,

00:01:33.746 --> 00:01:37.121
and in the last 15 years,
we’ve been able to have that,

00:01:37.121 --> 00:01:39.579
and that's partly what's enabled
all this progress.

00:01:39.954 --> 00:01:43.413
But at the same time,
I think we're doing several things wrong,

00:01:43.413 --> 00:01:45.413
and that's what I want
to talk to you about

00:01:45.454 --> 00:01:46.621
at the end of the talk.

00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:48.621
First, a bit of a history lesson.

00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:49.871
So for decades,

00:01:49.913 --> 00:01:52.038
almost since the very
beginning of computing,

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:54.329
people have wanted
to be able to build computers

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:58.246
that could see, understand language,
understand speech.

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:00.579
The earliest approaches
to this, generally,